  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CO-Support for Gaza Humanitarian Respons</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam supported the partner to finalize the log-frame and develop a MEAL plan. The partner conducted a baseline analysis at the start of the project and currently conducting and endline analysis to compare the results and achievements.
A MEAL officer and field coordinator were employed for the project at the partner organization and a main part of their role was to conduct continuous monitoring visits, satisfactory survey and to follow up feedback coming through the different mechanisms such as the hotline, community meetings and WhatsApp groups.
Oxfam conducted a number of monitoring visits and regular meetings with the management of Wefaq as well asthe project staff to follow up on the implementation and challenges faced by them and to discuss the possible solutions and recommendations.
A narrative and financial interim report is submitted by the partner quarterly as well as monthly progress updates. A final report will be submitted one month after the end of contract.
MAIN OBJECTIVE:
To increaseaccess for vulnerable women to safe, structured and coordinated multi-sectoral protection and GBV services in Rafah (including case management, psychosocial support, economic support and referrals to specialized service providers).
RESULTS:
Outcome: Increased access of 150 vulnerable women to safe, structured and coordinated multi-sectoral protection and GBV services in Rafah (including case management, psychosocial support, economicsupport and referrals to specialized service providers).
Outputs:
1.150 Women and girls survivors of GBV have access to psychosocial support services
2. 30 of the targeted women and girl survivors of GBV have access to legal support
3. 150 Women and girls survivors of GBV have access to in-kind support
4. 30 of the targeted women and girl survivors of GBV have access to case management services</narrative>
  </description>
